WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:04.390
You might know Michael B. Jordan from any
number of scene-stealing roles, like Steve

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:05.700
Montgomery in Chronicle…

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:06.520
"RRgh!

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:07.880
Steve Montgomery for President!"

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.720
...but chances are you've never seen him as
fit as he is in his most recent movies.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:16.890
The actor put on some serious muscle to convincingly
play the son of a legendary boxer in Creed

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:19.030
and a villainous revolutionary in Black Panther.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:20.500
So how did he get so swole?

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.480
Here's a look at how Michael B. Jordan got
ripped for Hollywood.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:25.040
Creed

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.740
While he's always been fit, Jordan had to
get seriously buff when he took the title

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.140
role of Adonis Creed in the 2015 boxing flick
Creed.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.360
Playing the son of legendary boxer Apollo
Creed from the Rocky films required Jordan

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.660
to take things to the next level, which he
did with the help of professional trainer

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:41.680
Corey Calliet.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.360
In order to properly portray a boxer, Jordan
had to train like a boxer.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:51.200
That meant 45-60 minutes daily of cardio along
with tons of ab workouts, like crunches, mountain

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:55.280
climbers, leg raises, reverse crunches, and
traditional sit-ups to build up his core and

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.120
burn fat.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:01.000
As for building muscle, Calliet had Jordan
focus on supersets — exercises where lifting

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:04.360
or curling dumbbells are interspersed with
push-ups or another workout.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:05.040
And after that?

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.120
Three full hours of boxing training.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:08.810
"This ain't your normal workout.

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.320
This is a Rocky style workout."

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.560
All told, Jordan packed on 24 pounds of pure
muscle over a year of training.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:16.780
According to Caillet, it was hard-going at
first:

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:21.040
"When we first started, he could barely bench
20 pounds, his legs were flailing everywhere

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.040
… he had nothing.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.240
He used to hate all this."

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:24.420
Jordan agreed, saying,

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:26.940
"I felt muscles I didn't even know I had."

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:30.570
It worked, though, so Jordan brought Caillet
along with him to help add another 20 pounds

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:34.540
of muscle in order to play the supervillain
Erik Killmonger in Black Panther.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.180
But that's not all Jordan did in order to
get ready for his big Marvel moment.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.520
Nutrition, nutrition, nutrition

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:45.160
As any fitness buff worth his salt will tell
you, exercise is only half the battle when

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:47.080
it comes to getting your body into peak shape.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:52.210
For Jordan to get into literal fighting condition,
he had to cut his food intake almost entirely

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:55.840
to lean proteins, carbs, green veggies, and
protein shakes.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:57.020
According to Jordan:

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.880
"I stripped down my diet completely."

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.510
"I worked out two to three times a day, six
days a week.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:05.500
And if you do that consistently for about
10 months, your body will change."

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:09.080
Don't worry, though, because on the seventh
day, Jordan rested, as Caillet allowed him

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:11.070
to cheat on his diet once a week with

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:14.960
"French toast in the morning, Philly cheesesteaks
in the afternoon, [and] pizza."

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:15.760
Yum!

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.980
Self-motivation is key

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:22.300
Jordan told Vice Sports he credits growing
up in Newark with a supportive family as the

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.840
inspiration for his work ethic and aspirations.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.580
"my dad used to tell me all the time, 'you
gotta be serious about something.'"

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:31.780
That motivation has been absolutely key to
Jordan's physical transformation, pushing

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:33.620
him to heavier weights and longer runs.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:37.680
No matter how painful the workout, Jordan
can persevere thanks to that motivation.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:42.100
"I told myself at a young age that I was gonna
sacrifice, I used to run myself into the ground

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:46.500
to like pure exhaustion because then I'd feel
like I oh I deserve it."

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:47.940
Also providing motivation?

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:48.840
The results.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:50.100
Jordan told Men's Fitness,

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.240
"You know, at first [...], you're hurting."

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:57.150
"When you start bench-pressing 225 pounds
10 times and it ain't nothing, and then you

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:59.630
start giving hugs to girls and they're, like,
feeling you up a little…"

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:02.500
"So I learned to love it when I started seeing
results."

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.360
Method Training

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.980
Being in fighting shape from Creed definitely
helped Jordan transition to the training for

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:12.260
Black Panther, where he used a new technique
called "Method Training."

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:16.060
The technique adapts Jordan's workouts to
match what his character would do to stay

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:18.800
in shape, helped alleviate the dreaded workout
boredom.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:23.350
Those workouts included a comprehensive weapons
training program in addition to learning various

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:24.720
forms of martial arts.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:28.460
For Jordan, it was a real departure from the
boxing-focused training of Creed.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:29.820
Jordan told Collider,

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.680
"This one is more martial arts, using a lot
of your legs, so I'm picking up different

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.680
fighting styles.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:38.020
Also a lot of guns too, the weapons training
is a totally different muscle."

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:40.180
No rest for the wickedly fit

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:44.510
While any normal person might want to take
a break from nonstop workout routines and

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:48.740
just eat some pizza and drink some beer, Jordan
is jumping right back into training for Creed

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:49.240
2.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:53.660
The story will follow Adonis Creed fighting
the son of Ivan Drago, the man who killed

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:55.740
Apollo Creed in the ring in Rocky IV.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:01.420
Professional boxer Florian Munteanu will be
playing the son of Ivan Drago, and at 6 foot

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:04.280
4 and 245 pounds, Jordan has his work cut
out for him.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:08.280
But if there's one thing his training has
proven so far, it's that Jordan isn't afraid

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:09.400
of a little hard work.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:10.400
Thanks for watching!

